Description: low-latency viewer for USB HDMI capture devices
 LLCV shows video and audio from UVC (V4L2) HDMI capture devices such as
 the AVerMedia Live Gamer ULTRA S GC553 with minimal delay. Only the newest
 captured frame is presented, using OpenGL for color conversion and
 scaling, and capture audio is played through PipeWire with a small
 drift-corrected buffer.
 .
 Features include NV12, YUY2, MJPEG, BGR24 and P010 (HDR10) capture modes,
 HDR10 passthrough on Wayland compositors with color management, HDR to SDR
 tone mapping everywhere else, immediate or VSync presentation, an
 audio-only mode, PNG screenshots at the capture resolution and a live
 diagnostics overlay. It runs on Wayland by default and can also use X11
 (XWayland), with Mesa (AMD, Intel) and NVIDIA OpenGL drivers.
 .
 P010 capture needs Linux 7.1 or newer, or a uvcvideo module with P010
 support. On releases without SDL3, such as Ubuntu 24.04, SDL3 is built
 into the program (build profile pkg.llcv.bundled-sdl3).
